{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the wraps.</b> These are garments, like \"and take his garment\" (II Samuel 2:21):" "<b>And the veils.</b> Some say: a garment with which the woman wraps herself. And some say: the wraps are tunics and the veils are breeches." "<b>And the kerchiefs.</b> Like \"bring the kerchief that is on you\" (Ruth 3:15):" "<b>And the headbands.</b> Some say: like the form of a טלית, close to the language of Ishmael. Or it is from the root of בחרט אנוש (Isaiah 8:1), as I shall yet explain."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:22.795564648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}